    </node>
    <node id="UN&#205;PAROS">
      <data key="d0">REPRODUCTION</data>
      <data key="d1">Un&#237;paros is a term used to describe mammals that give birth to a single offspring at a time, such as the elephant seal.</data>
      <data key="d2">b58cdc05bb2d9dbcf563d7eaa562cf0f</data>
      <data key="d6">110</data>
      <data key="d7">2</data>
      <data key="d3">1</data>
      <data key="d4">95</data>
      <data key="d5">9ecd6765668446dab1ad6f2462811025</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PER&#205;ODO DE GESTACI&#211;N">
      <data key="d0">REPRODUCTION</data>
      <data key="d1">The period of gestation is the length of time between conception and birth, which is around 340 days for the elephant seal.</data>
      <data key="d2">b58cdc05bb2d9dbcf563d7eaa562cf0f</data>
      <data key="d6">110</data>
      <data key="d7">2</data>
      <data key="d3">1</data>
      <data key="d4">96</data>
      <data key="d5">17be16159a2246fc8604a0b19279d570</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ALUMBRAMIENTOS GEMELARES">
      <data key="d0">REPRODUCTION</data>
      <data key="d1">Alumbramientos gemelares is a term used to describe the rare case of giving birth to two offspring at once, which is not common in elephant seals.</data>
      <data key="d2">b58cdc05bb2d9dbcf563d7eaa562cf0f</data>
      <data key="d6">110</data>
      <data key="d7">2</data>
      <data key="d3">1</data>
      <data key="d4">97</data>
      <data key="d5">186edd79de6b44609632c7d8dd6dd046</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LAPSO &#193;LGIDO DE ALUMBRAMIENTOS">
      <data key="d0">REPRODUCTION</data>
      <data key="d1">The lapso &#225;lgido de alumbramientos is the period of time during which most births occur, which is from January 15 to 25 for the elephant seal.</data>
      <data key="d2">b58cdc05bb2d9dbcf563d7eaa562cf0f</data>
      <data key="d6">110</data>
      <data key="d7">2</data>
      <data key="d3">1</data>
      <data key="d4">98</data>
      <data key="d5">adcc2d8136354c2a95271899694d846f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PRIMEROS NACIMIENTOS">
      <data key="d0">REPRODUCTION</data>
      <data key="d1">The first births refer to the earliest recorded births during the alumbramiento period, which occur around mid-December for the elephant seal.</data>
      <data key="d2">b58cdc05bb2d9dbcf563d7eaa562cf0f</data>
      <data key="d6">110</data>
      <data key="d7">2</data>
      <data key="d3">1</data>
      <data key="d4">99</data>
      <data key="d5">de6023ffb7e84f239104ce3c1eb8dcc3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&#218;LTIMOS NACIMIENTOS">
      <data key="d0">REPRODUCTION</data>
      <data key="d1">The &#250;ltimos nacimientos refer to the latest recorded births during the alumbramiento period, which occur around the first half of February for the elephant seal.</data>
      <data key="d2">b58cdc05bb2d9dbcf563d7eaa562cf0f</data>
      <data key="d6">110</data>
      <data key="d7">2</data>
      <data key="d3">1</data>
      <data key="d4">100</data>
      <data key="d5">521a004c9e734a28912811b9dfb1b4b9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EXCITABILIDAD">
      <data key="d0">BEHAVIOR</data>
      <data key="d1">Excitabilidad is a term used to describe the heightened state of awareness or reactivity in an animal, such as the increased excitability of a female elephant seal before giving birth.</data>
      <data key="d2">b58cdc05bb2d9dbcf563d7eaa562cf0f</data>
      <data key="d6">35</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
      <data key="d3">1</data>
      <data key="d4">101</data>
      <data key="d5">88669182631d42cebd9a2e0b1feeaa02</data>
    </node>
    <node id="RI&#209;AS">
      <data key="d0">BEHAVIOR</data>
      <data key="d1">Ri&#241;as is a term used to describe conflicts or fights between animals, which can occur between female elephant seals before giving birth.</data>
      <data key="d2">b58cdc05bb2d9dbcf563d7eaa562cf0f</data>
      <data key="d6">35</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
      <data key="d3">1</data>
      <data key="d4">102</data>
      <data key="d5">577ad5042a944ffb9c2c59350c7c3cfc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="C&#218;BITO-VENTRAL">
      <data key="d0">BEHAVIOR</data>
      <data key="d1">C&#250;bito-ventral is a term used to describe a resting position in which the animal lies on its side with its belly facing downward, which is a common position for pregnant female elephant seals before giving birth.</data>
      <data key="d2">b58cdc05bb2d9dbcf563d7eaa562cf0f</data>
      <data key="d6">35</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
      <data key="d3">1</data>
      <data key="d4">103</data>
      <data key="d5">c85f511fceb84361affb23c7be789da7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="INTENSO LAGRIMEO">
      <data key="d0">BIOLOGICAL CHARACTERISTICS</data>
      <data key="d1">Intenso lagrimeo is a term used to describe excessive tearing or eye secretion, which is a sign of advanced pregnancy in female elephant seals.</data>
      <data key="d2">b58cdc05bb2d9dbcf563d7eaa562cf0f</data>
      <data key="d6">35</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
      <data key="d3">1</data>
      <data key="d4">104</data>
      <data key="d5">9dd1f2ec517d4615884f7915456968ba</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TREN POSTERIOR">
      <data key="d0">BIOLOGICAL CHARACTERISTICS</data>
      <data key="d1">Tren posterior is a term used to describe the hindquarters or back end of an animal, which is used as a point of support by female elephant seals during labor.</data>
      <data key="d2">b58cdc05bb2d9dbcf563d7eaa562cf0f</data>
      <data key="d6">35</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
      <data key="d3">1</data>
      <data key="d4">105</data>
      <data key="d5">e82ca58ea854426db235e9151a82dec3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PARTO">
      <data key="d0">REPRODUCTION</data>
      <data key="d1"> El t&#233;rmino "parto" se refiere al proceso por el cual la loba del lobo marino da a luz a su cr&#237;a, el cual dura aproximadamente 4 minutos. Despu&#233;s del parto, la cr&#237;a se amamanta hasta los seis meses de edad. A pesar de que el texto menciona al elefante marino en la descripci&#243;n, el foco de la informaci&#243;n se centra en el lobo marino, espec&#237;ficamente en su proceso de parto y los cuidados maternos posteriores.</data>
      <data key="d2">34798580ffa1eeacedf7b69c5f9ef85d,a7319504eeb762ae0cc5b15c4d6b5461,b58cdc05bb2d9dbcf563d7eaa562cf0f</data>
      <data key="d6">86</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
      <data key="d3">3</data>
      <data key="d4">106</data>
      <data key="d5">30973ec7c970494ba157ca83042c5b6f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BOLSA">
      <data key="d0">BIOLOGICAL CHARACTERISTICS</data>
      <data key="d1">Bolsa is a term used to describe the placenta and other membranes that surround the fetus in utero, which are expelled during the birth process in elephant seals.</data>
      <data key="d2">b58cdc05bb2d9dbcf563d7eaa562cf0f</data>
      <data key="d6">35</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
      <data key="d3">1</data>
      <data key="d4">107</data>
      <data key="d5">55ec634d1944466285f457fc661c4702</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ESCISI&#211;N DEL CORD&#211;N UMBILICAL">
      <data key="d0">REPRODUCTION</data>
      <data key="d1">Escisi&#243;n del cord&#243;n umbilical is a term used to describe the separation of the umbilical cord from the newborn, which occurs involuntarily in elephant seals as a result of the mother's movements.</data>
      <data key="d2">b58cdc05bb2d9dbcf563d7eaa562cf0f</data>
      <data key="d6">35</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
      <data key="d3">1</data>
      <data key="d4">108</data>
      <data key="d5">3eb8f01b9d884809846ddc4ee51c0236</data>
    </node>
