    <node id="ISLA RASA">
      <data key="d0">HABITAT</data>
      <data key="d1"> Isla Rasa is a low-altitude, rocky island located to the east-southeast of Cabo Dos Bah&#237;as and northwest of Cabo de Matas. Its coasts are smooth and devoid of vegetation, with the entire surface of the island, particularly the center and northwest coast, serving as a habitat for a population of 6,500 single-furred sea lions.</data>
      <data key="d2">5a07380f5aada9c6c6ef41f242e1c536,6d318de28f93d9164e886cc7489e0e83,882fdf01528bf45b0f6d55ba9924f551</data>
