    <node id="ISLA ESCONDIDA">
      <data key="d0">HABITAT</data>
      <data key="d1"> Isla Escondida is a geographical location in the Pen&#237;nsula Vald&#233;s, specifically in the northern region, and is known for being the home to a significant colony of two-haired sea lions. It is one of the two places where extra-continental colonies of two-haired sea lions can be found. Isla Escondida has an estimated population of 250 sea lions and is recognized for its biodiversity, as well as its importance in the conservation of pinnipeds, making it a significant location in the marine science community.</data>
      <data key="d2">2d041f866c2a7f149216961d43696c82,45abddc2bb9e83effafbcae15de72d03,8a0c5d2be39b9a9e02f97cbc7551030c,acce0f2d52d35b868047d606555fc1e4</data>
      <data key="d6">59</data>
