    <node id="BARRANCAS">
      <data key="d0">BIOLOGICAL CHARACTERISTICS</data>
      <data key="d1"> "Barrancas" are coastal geological formations of little height that offer protection and refuge to local fauna, particularly to marine birds. They serve as nesting and breeding sites for marine birds. Specifically, they are a key geographical feature of "Punta Norte" sea lion colony, where sea lions reproduce and rest.</data>
      <data key="d2">3b8a637af69ae3ba996edaf49f1ed1f0,a601887e8e26ca24bc383e59ed0bd947,b936698b8bf77875919870e3152faf6d</data>
