    </node>
    <node id="ISLOTE SUR DE PUNTA LOBER&#205;A">
      <data key="d0">HABITAT</data>
      <data key="d1"> "Islote Sur de Punta Lober&#237;a is a permanent, mixed, and breeding habitat for the two-headed sea lions, located in Bah&#237;a Vera and also known as Isla Cumbre. It is a low-altitude rocky islet, devoid of vegetation, situated to the south and facing Punta Lober&#237;a, with an approximate size of 270 meters in length and 180 meters in width. The area is described as both estacional and inexplotado, indicating that it may experience changes in conditions and has not been exploited."</data>
      <data key="d2">cf58f0416a8d27360f6d6e772471b831,d12aea8b41f8654da913712b1182332f</data>
      <data key="d6">21</data>
