    <node id="UBICACI&#211;N GEOGR&#193;FICA">
      <data key="d0">NONE</data>
      <data key="d1"> The "UBICACI&#211;N GEOGR&#193;FICA" (geographic location) of the entities are as follows: Isla Rasa is located to the E.S.E. of Cabo Dos Bah&#237;as and to the N.W. of Cabo de Matas, with an approximate distance of 12 nautical miles and 9.5 nautical miles respectively. The island is oriented in a N.W. to S.E. direction, spanning 750 meters in length and 180 meters in width in a N.E. to S.W. direction.

Islote Gran Robredo is situated to the North of Golfo San Jorge and to the S.W. of Isla Tova, with an approximate distance of 7500 meters between the S.W. end of the islet and the N.W. point of Isla Tova. Its latitude is 45&#176; 7&#8217; 57&#8221; S and its longitude is 66&#176; 3&#8217; 34&#8221; W.

Islote Puntudo can be found to the W.S.W. of Punta Medanosa and to the north of Bah&#237;a de los Nodales, located 1600 meters from the coast. Its latitude is 48&#176; 7&#8217; 3&#8221; S and its longitude is 66&#176; 3&#8217; 12&#8221; W.

There is no provided information on the geographic location of the island Moreno.

There is no provided information on the geographic location of the island Vald&#233;s.

There is no provided information on the geographic location of the islote sur de Punta Lober&#237;a.</data>
      <data key="d2">6d318de28f93d9164e886cc7489e0e83,94f4298857de42f37006e6e3561c06ee,d12aea8b41f8654da913712b1182332f</data>
      <data key="d6">118</data>
      <data key="d7">2</data>
      <data key="d3">1</data>
      <data key="d4">314</data>
      <data key="d5">af0c5636d3134fcf85d7f3a181c0693a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TOPOGRAF&#205;A REGIONAL">
      <data key="d0">NONE</data>
      <data key="d1"> La topograf&#237;a regional de la regi&#243;n que rodea a un islote se caracteriza por una forma y caracter&#237;sticas geogr&#225;ficas espec&#237;ficas. En el caso de Isla Rasa, la topograf&#237;a es de baja altura, con costas suaves y sin vegetaci&#243;n. La lober&#237;a ocupa la mayor parte de la superficie de la isla, especialmente el centro y la costa N.W.

El Islote Gran Robredo presenta una topograf&#237;a regional diferente, con un islote rocoso de alguna altura, costas bajas y una poblaci&#243;n lobera que se concentra en la regi&#243;n S.W. del tercer islote.

El Islote Puntudo tiene una topograf&#237;a regional que incluye un islote rocoso de escasa altura, con costas que proyectan restinga, sin vegetaci&#243;n y de color blanco amarillento.

La topograf&#237;a regional de la isla Moreno y la isla Vald&#233;s no se especifica en los datos proporcionados, pero se menciona que forman parte de la regi&#243;n.

Por &#250;ltimo, la topograf&#237;a regional del islote sur de Punta Lober&#237;a no se describe en detalle, pero se menciona como parte de la regi&#243;n de estudio.</data>
      <data key="d2">53907ffc5477638e3f3aba25eaddf038,6d318de28f93d9164e886cc7489e0e83,94f4298857de42f37006e6e3561c06ee,d12aea8b41f8654da913712b1182332f</data>
      <data key="d6">120</data>
      <data key="d7">2</data>
      <data key="d3">2</data>
      <data key="d4">315</data>
      <data key="d5">9cf9302be56b425abb72fa0d6c8bebb7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CARACTER&#205;STICAS">
      <data key="d0">NONE</data>
      <data key="d1"> The "CARACTER&#205;STICAS" include the distinctive features of Isla Moreno and Isla Vald&#233;s, as well as the properties of a described islote, which can be found in the southern part of Punta Lober&#237;a. The features of the islas and islote consist of physical and ecological traits. Moreover, the "CARACTER&#205;STICAS" encompass the characteristics of populations of sea lions, which can be categorized as permanent, mixed, or pupping, with details about their type, duration, and population. Lastly, the "CARACTER&#205;STICAS" also describe the lober&#237;a, which includes features of the sea lion colony, such as its type, duration, and population.</data>
      <data key="d2">12514c85e508ab1f8e976632806d74d6,53907ffc5477638e3f3aba25eaddf038,d12aea8b41f8654da913712b1182332f,e411653fa84230bcd9ca8f9b38657cca</data>
