      <data key="d5">c96945b0d15d4d19942ed322c814d651</data>
    </node>
    <node id="POBLACI&#211;N">
      <data key="d0">NONE</data>
      <data key="d1"> The entity "POBLACI&#211;N" (population) refers to the number of sea lions in different categories, including the total, males, females, and young individuals. This population can be found inhabiting specific areas, such as the islet Moreno and islet Vald&#233;s. Moreover, the population is also studied in the context of different lober&#237;as, including Punta Lober&#237;a's southern islet. In all these cases, the population is analyzed considering the different age and sex categories of sea lions. Therefore, "POBLACI&#211;N" refers to the number of sea lions, including T.M. (presumably total males), H. (presumably hembras or females), M. (presumably machos or males), and L. (presumably lobos or sea lions) in each of the lober&#237;as mentioned in the text.</data>
      <data key="d2">12514c85e508ab1f8e976632806d74d6,53907ffc5477638e3f3aba25eaddf038,a48ce0dd8016f44c624e3bc01162c4c5,d12aea8b41f8654da913712b1182332f,e411653fa84230bcd9ca8f9b38657cca</data>
      <data key="d6">64</data>
