    <node id="CARACTER&#205;STICAS: PERMANENTE, MIXTO, PARICI&#211;N.">
      <data key="d0">BIOLOGICAL CHARACTERISTICS</data>
      <data key="d1"> The entities "CARACTER&#205;STICAS: PERMANENTE, MIXTO, PARICI&#211;N" are related to the characteristics of two marine habitats, specifically Isla Rasa and Islote Gran Robredo. According to the descriptions, both of these marine locations share the same characteristics: they are permanent, mixed-use habitats and serve as a place of parturition for a colony of sea lions. The term "permanente" suggests that these habitats are stable and always present, while "mixto" indicates that they are used by multiple species or for multiple purposes. The term "parici&#243;n" refers to the act of giving birth, specifically to the sea lion pups born in these colonies. Therefore, a comprehensive summary of the data provided would be:

Isla Rasa and Islote Gran Robredo are two marine habitats that share the same characteristics: they are permanent, mixed-use habitats and serve as a place of parturition for a colony of sea lions.</data>
      <data key="d2">6d318de28f93d9164e886cc7489e0e83</data>
      <data key="d3">0</data>
      <data key="d4">335</data>
      <data key="d5">d10622952dd043bebd4b04c71d2eea69</data>
    </node>
