    <edge source="AVES GUAN&#205;FERAS" target="PHALACROCORACIDEOS">
      <data key="d8">18.0</data>
      <data key="d9"> "AVES GUAN&#205;FERAS and PHALACROCORACIDEOS both include and are part of the larger category of bird species."</data>
      <data key="d10">3b8a637af69ae3ba996edaf49f1ed1f0</data>
      <data key="d11">0067c183f60e4c3dabe884152bf020b7</data>
      <data key="d12">749</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="AVES GUAN&#205;FERAS" target="PELECANIFORMES">
      <data key="d8">18.0</data>
      <data key="d9"> "AVES GUAN&#205;FERAS incluye a, mientras que PELECANIFORMES pertenece a, diferentes grupos de aves marinas. La primera se refiere a aves marinas que se alimentan principalmente de plantas, como los loros de mar, mientras que la segunda agrupa a las aves con pico en forma de saco, como los pel&#237;canos y las fragatas."</data>
      <data key="d10">3b8a637af69ae3ba996edaf49f1ed1f0</data>
      <data key="d11">8ac12c9861664caf9933c1256ca932d3</data>
      <data key="d12">750</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="AVES GUAN&#205;FERAS" target="CORMOR&#193;N DE MAGALLANES">
      <data key="d8">18.0</data>
      <data key="d9"> "AVES GUAN&#201;FORAS" are a group of species, while "CORMOR&#193;N DE MAGALLANES" is a specific species included within the group of "AVES GUAN&#201;FORAS". Therefore, the comprehensive summary would be: "Los CORMOR&#193;NES DE MAGALLANES son una especie incluida en el grupo de AVES GUAN&#201;FORAS".</data>
      <data key="d10">3b8a637af69ae3ba996edaf49f1ed1f0</data>
      <data key="d11">d484457dfc4a41ad9e5d0438ba0e7695</data>
      <data key="d12">751</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="AVES GUAN&#205;FERAS" target="CORMOR&#193;N GRIS">
      <data key="d8">18.0</data>
      <data key="d9"> "AVES GUAN&#201;FORAS" and "CORMOR&#193;N GRIS" are both species that are part of the larger group of marine birds. While "AVES GUAN&#201;FORAS" is a general term that includes several species of marine birds, "CORMOR&#193;N GRIS" is a specific species within that group.</data>
      <data key="d10">3b8a637af69ae3ba996edaf49f1ed1f0</data>
      <data key="d11">c86b4d6850494361b99b29fab4a52c7a</data>
      <data key="d12">752</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="AVES GUAN&#205;FERAS" target="CORMOR&#193;N">
      <data key="d8">18.0</data>
      <data key="d9"> "AVES GUAN&#201;FORAS" and "CORMOR&#193;N" are both entities related to the field of marine ecology. AVES GUAN&#201;FORAS (which can be translated to "Boobies" in English) is a type of seabird species, while CORMOR&#193;N (Cormorant) is a genus of seabirds that includes various species. Therefore, it can be said that CORMOR&#193;N is one of the entities that are included in the broader category of AVES GUAN&#201;FORAS.</data>
      <data key="d10">3b8a637af69ae3ba996edaf49f1ed1f0</data>
      <data key="d11">688128aadfcd4c3ca927599ea0b8a2a1</data>
      <data key="d12">753</data>
      <data key="d13">2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="AVES GUAN&#205;FERAS" target="GUANO DE AVES MARINAS">
      <data key="d8">10.0</data>
      <data key="d9"> "AVES GUAN&#205;FERAS, also known as seabirds, generate guano, which is referred to as GUANO DE AVES MARINAS. This guano is a product of the seabirds' natural processes."</data>
      <data key="d10">3b8a637af69ae3ba996edaf49f1ed1f0</data>
      <data key="d11">06dac701b6124c45a8f63b9824ef55cc</data>
